Charis
Copyright 2026 HARTLE.TECH (NIPC 518241327, Porto, Portugal)

A motion and material library for Qt Quick, and a visual builder whose output
is ordinary code. Named for Charis, the Greek personification of grace — which
is the whole brief: the difference between a UI that moves and one that moves
well.

Charis supplies the four things Qt Quick does not: spring motion integrated
against real frame time, continuous-curvature corners, a single shared frame
clock so an idle interface draws nothing, and an adaptive frame budget.

